# The emitter writes LF, and the gallery check compares its output against the
# committed scripts byte for byte. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites all fifteen to CRLF and every one of them fails a
# check that has nothing to do with line endings. CI runs on Linux, so it never
# sees this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Content detection guesses these right, but a wrong guess corrupts them, and
# the gallery is committed on purpose.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.gif binary
